  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0379, and it contains five tables: Customer, Invoice, Terms, Invoice_and_Customer, and Invoice_and_Terms.\nThe Customer table has five columns: Contact_Information, Contact_Person, Customer_Address, Customer_ID (primary key), and Customer_Name. The Customer_ID column is an integer and is the primary key.\nThe Invoice table has ten columns: Customer_ID (foreign key referencing Customer), Due_Date, Electronic_Version_Content, Electronic_Version_MIME_Type, Invoice_Date, Invoice_ID (primary key), Notes, Payment_Amount, Payment_Date, Status, and Total_Amount. The Invoice_ID column is an integer and is the primary key. The Customer_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Customer table.\nThe Terms table has four columns: Interest_Rate, Invoice_ID (foreign key referencing Invoice), Payment_Days, and Term_Description. The Term_ID column is an integer and is the primary key. The Invoice_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Invoice table.\nThe Invoice_and_Customer table has ten columns: Customer_ID (foreign key referencing Customer), Due_Date, Electronic_Version_Content, Electronic_Version_MIME_Type, Invoice_Date, Invoice_ID (foreign key referencing Invoice), Notes, Payment_Amount, Payment_Date, Status, and Total_Amount. The primary key is a composite of Invoice_ID and Customer_ID. The Customer_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Customer table, and the Invoice_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Invoice table.\nThe Invoice_and_Terms table has five columns: Interest_Rate, Invoice_ID (foreign key referencing Invoice), Payment_Days, Term_Description, and Term_ID (foreign key referencing Terms). The primary key is a composite of Term_ID and Invoice_ID. The Invoice_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Invoice table, and the Term_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Terms table.\nIn summary, this schema contains five tables that represent customers, invoices, terms, invoices and customers, and invoices and terms. Each table has its own set of columns, and there are foreign key relationships between the tables. The primary keys and foreign keys are used to enforce entity and referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Requirement Description:\nA financial management system for managing invoices. The main functions include managing invoice information, such as creating, updating, and querying invoices. Invoice information includes Invoice ID, Invoice Date, Due Date, Total Amount, Status, Notes, Payment Date, Payment Amount, MIME Type of the Electronic Version, and Content of the Electronic Version. It also associates with customer information to track which customer each invoice belongs to. Additionally, it associates with terms information to manage different payment terms for invoices.\nManaging customer information, where each customer has a unique Customer ID, Customer Name, Customer Address, Contact Person, and Contact Information.\nManaging terms information, including Term ID, Term Description, Payment Days, and Interest Rate.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0379.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0379\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `due_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `electronic_version_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `electronic_version_mime_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`),\n  KEY `fk_customer` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `terms` (\n  `term_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `interest_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_days` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `term_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`term_id`),\n  KEY `fk_invoice` (`invoice_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `terms_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invoice_id`) REFERENCES `invoice` (`invoice_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice_and_customer` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `due_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `invoice_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `electronic_version_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `electronic_version_mime_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`, `customer_id`),\n  KEY `fk_customer_2` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `fk_invoice_2` (`invoice_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_and_customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_and_customer_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`invoice_id`) REFERENCES `invoice` (`invoice_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice_and_terms` (\n  `term_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `interest_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_days` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `term_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`term_id`, `invoice_id`),\n  KEY `fk_invoice_3` (`invoice_id`),\n  KEY `fk_terms` (`term_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_and_terms_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invoice_id`) REFERENCES `invoice` (`invoice_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_and_terms_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`term_id`) REFERENCES `terms` (`term_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
